    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Pros first: easy fresh-fruit snack. It works with no peeling or cooking, so it is easy to use when the fruit is ripe. Peel adds tart colour. Keeping the skin gives more plum colour, texture, and sharp-sweet contrast. Works fresh or cooked. It can go into yoghurt, oats, salads, compote, sauces, or desserts without much effort.",
      "textSha256": "91198086576c2298e4aa0236c78bf65c844df6d4daf40227ecc52203d8865135",
      "characterCount": 327,
      "byteLength": 402956,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 25.156,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/plums/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "ae1b08ZifqZCuPww6zFw",
        "historyItemId": "91F7yelRBJRt1jhpfXOp"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/plums/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: bruises easily. Soft fruit bruises quickly, so quality can drop fast after transport or storage. Ripeness window is short. The best eating window is narrow, and underripe or overripe plums are much less useful. Stone interrupts snacking. The pit makes them less convenient than fully edible bite-size fruit like berries or grapes.",
      "textSha256": "da54e4483729250064bc8d4d8e7a6d150300cbef9d9ae73a9f44aeeb4879597e",
      "characterCount": 341,
      "byteLength": 436393,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 27.246,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/plums/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "uLSYcloFWedPcThUR8tG",
        "historyItemId": "koa87zDNcYARmUrzQyBr"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/plums/voice/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are that it's an easy fresh-fruit snack and low glycemic index. Weak spots are low fiber and low vitamin A. Best for quick on the go snacks, low-calorie to volume ratio, and its ability to compliment many other foods.",
